{"id":"mahabharata-6-092","work":"mahabharata","part":6,"partName":"भीष्मपर्व","partNameEn":"Bhishma Parva","unit":92,"title":"द्विनवतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 92 · Arjuna's grief and the eighth night","summary":{"en":"Hearing of Iravan's death, Arjuna is sunk in grief and recalls Vidura's warning. He kills many of the Kaurava brothers, Abhimanyu fights fiercely, and at nightfall both armies withdraw.","kn":"ಇರಾವಾನನ ಮರಣ ಕೇಳಿ ಅರ್ಜುನ ದುಃಖದಲ್ಲಿ ಮುಳುಗಿ ವಿದುರನ ಎಚ್ಚರಿಕೆಯನ್ನು ನೆನೆಯುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಅನೇಕ ಕೌರವ ತಮ್ಮಂದಿರನ್ನು ಕೊಲ್ಲುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಅಭಿಮನ್ಯು ಉಗ್ರವಾಗಿ ಹೋರಾಡುತ್ತಾನೆ; ರಾತ್ರಿಯಲ್ಲಿ ಎರಡೂ ಸೈನ್ಯಗಳು ಹಿಂದೆ ಸರಿಯುತ್ತವೆ.","hi":"इरावान् की मृत्यु सुनकर अर्जुन शोक में डूब जाते हैं और विदुर की चेतावनी याद करते हैं। वे कई कौरव भाइयों को मारते हैं, अभिमन्यु उग्र युद्ध करता है, और रात होने पर दोनों सेनाएँ लौट जाती हैं।","te":"ఇరావంతుని మరణం విని అర్జునుడు దుఃఖంలో మునిగి విదురుని హెచ్చరికను గుర్తు చేసుకుంటాడు. అనేక కౌరవ సోదరులను చంపుతాడు, అభిమన్యుడు భీకరంగా పోరాడతాడు; రాత్రికి ఇరు సేనలు వెనుదిరుగుతాయి.","ta":"இராவானின் மரணம் கேட்டு அர்ஜுனன் துயரில் மூழ்கி விதுரனின் எச்சரிக்கையை நினைக்கிறான். பல கௌரவ சகோதரரைக் கொல்கிறான், அபிமன்யு கடுமையாகப் போரிடுகிறான்; இரவில் இரு படைகளும் பின்வாங்குகின்றன.","ml":"ഇരാവന്റെ മരണവാർത്ത കേട്ട് അർജുനൻ ദുഃഖത്തിൽ മുങ്ങുന്നു; വിദുരരുടെ മുന്നറിയിപ്പ് അദ്ദേഹം ഓർക്കുന്നു. അദ്ദേഹം കൗരവ സഹോദരന്മാരിൽ പലരെയും വധിക്കുന്നു; അഭിമന്യു ഘോരമായി പൊരുതുന്നു; രാത്രിയായപ്പോൾ ഇരുസേനകളും പിൻവാങ്ങുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 6.92; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 26 2021","sections":[{"title":"भीष्मवधपर्व","titleEn":"Bhishmavadha Parva (The fall of Bhishma)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"पुत्रं तु निहतं श्रुत्वा इरावन्तं धनंजयः ।\nदुःखेन महताविष्टो निःश्वसन्पन्नगो यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing that his son Iravan had been slain, Arjuna was seized by great sorrow and sighed like a serpent."}},{"n":2,"text":"अब्रवीत्समरे राजन्वासुदेवमिदं वचः ।\nइदं नूनं महाप्राज्ञो विदुरो दृष्टवान्पुरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"O king, he spoke these words to Vasudeva in the battle: \"Surely the wise Vidura foresaw this long ago."}},{"n":3,"text":"कुरूणां पाण्डवानां च क्षयं घोरं महामतिः ।\nततो निवारयितवान्धृतराष्ट्रं जनेश्वरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the dreadful ruin of the Kurus and the Pandavas, that far-sighted man tried to hold King Dhritarashtra back from this war."}},{"n":4,"text":"अवध्या बहवो वीराः संग्रामे मधुसूदन ।\nनिहताः कौरवैः संख्ये तथास्माभिश्च ते हताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Slayer of Madhu, many warriors who ought not to be killed are being killed in battle, struck down by the Kauravas, and slain by us as well."}},{"n":5,"text":"अर्थहेतोर्नरश्रेष्ठ क्रियते कर्म कुत्सितम् ।\nधिगर्थान्यत्कृते ह्येवं क्रियते ज्ञातिसंक्षयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of men, it is for wealth that this shameful deed is done. Curse wealth, for whose sake kinsmen are being destroyed!"}},{"n":6,"text":"अधनस्य मृतं श्रेयो न च ज्ञातिवधाद्धनम् ।\nकिं नु प्राप्स्यामहे कृष्ण हत्वा ज्ञातीन्समागतान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"For a man without wealth, death is better, and wealth won by killing kinsmen is worthless. Krishna, what shall we gain by slaying these relatives gathered here?"}},{"n":7,"text":"दुर्योधनापराधेन शकुनेः सौबलस्य च ।\nक्षत्रिया निधनं यान्ति कर्णदुर्मन्त्रितेन च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Because of the fault of Duryodhana and of Shakuni, son of Subala, and because of Karna's evil counsel, the Kshatriyas are meeting their deaths."}},{"n":8,"text":"इदानीं च विजानामि सुकृतं मधुसूदन ।\nकृतं राज्ञा महाबाहो याचता स्म सुयोधनम् ।\nराज्यार्धं पञ्च वा ग्रामान्नाकार्षीत्स च दुर्मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Now I understand, Madhusudana, how well the king acted when he begged Suyodhana for half the kingdom, or even just five villages. That fool refused."}},{"n":9,"text":"दृष्ट्वा हि क्षत्रियाञ्शूराञ्शयानान्धरणीतले ।\nनिन्दामि भृशमात्मानं धिगस्तु क्षत्रजीविकाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the brave Kshatriyas lying on the ground, I blame myself bitterly. Shame on the livelihood of a warrior!"}},{"n":10,"text":"अशक्तमिति मामेते ज्ञास्यन्ति क्षत्रिया रणे ।\nयुद्धं ममैभिरुचितं ज्ञातिभिर्मधुसूदन ॥","meaning":{"en":"These Kshatriyas will think me weak in battle, yet this war was chosen by my kinsmen, Madhusudana."}},{"n":11,"text":"संचोदय हयान्क्षिप्रं धार्तराष्ट्रचमूं प्रति ।\nप्रतरिष्ये महापारं भुजाभ्यां समरोदधिम् ।\nनायं क्लीबयितुं कालो विद्यते माधव क्वचित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drive the horses quickly toward the army of Dhritarashtra's sons. With my arms I will cross this vast ocean of battle. Madhava, this is no time to be unmanned.\""}},{"n":12,"text":"एवमुक्तस्तु पार्थेन केशवः परवीरहा ।\nचोदयामास तानश्वान्पाण्डुरान्वातरंहसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed by Partha, Keshava, slayer of enemy heroes, urged on the white horses that ran swift as the wind."}},{"n":13,"text":"अथ शब्दो महानासीत्तव सैन्यस्य भारत ।\nमारुतोद्धूतवेगस्य सागरस्येव पर्वणि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, Bharata, a great roar rose from your army, like the sea surging on a full-moon day when lashed by the wind."}},{"n":14,"text":"अपराह्णे महाराज संग्रामः समपद्यत ।\nपर्जन्यसमनिर्घोषो भीष्मस्य सह पाण्डवैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the afternoon, great king, the fighting between Bhishma and the Pandavas began, resounding like thunder."}},{"n":15,"text":"ततो राजंस्तव सुता भीमसेनमुपाद्रवन् ।\nपरिवार्य रणे द्रोणं वसवो वासवं यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O king, your sons rushed upon Bhimasena, surrounding him as the Vasus surround Indra, while others surrounded Drona in the battle."}},{"n":16,"text":"ततः शांतनवो भीष्मः कृपश्च रथिनां वरः ।\nभगदत्तः सुशर्मा च धनंजयमुपाद्रवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Bhishma son of Shantanu, Kripa best of charioteers, Bhagadatta, and Susharma rushed upon Dhananjaya."}},{"n":17,"text":"हार्दिक्यो बाह्लिकश्चैव सात्यकिं समभिद्रुतौ ।\nअम्बष्ठकस्तु नृपतिरभिमन्युमवारयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hardikya Kritavarman and Bahlika charged at Satyaki, and the king of the Ambashthas held Abhimanyu back."}},{"n":18,"text":"शेषास्त्वन्ये महाराज शेषानेव महारथान् ।\nततः प्रववृते युद्धं घोररूपं भयावहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The remaining warriors, great king, engaged the remaining great chariot-fighters, and a terrible, fearful battle began."}},{"n":19,"text":"भीमसेनस्तु संप्रेक्ष्य पुत्रांस्तव जनेश्वर ।\nप्रजज्वाल रणे क्रुद्धो हविषा हव्यवाडिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing your sons, Bhimasena blazed up in rage on the battlefield, like a fire fed with the oblation."}},{"n":20,"text":"पुत्रास्तु तव कौन्तेयं छादयां चक्रिरे शरैः ।\nप्रावृषीव महाराज जलदाः पर्वतं यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your sons covered the son of Kunti with arrows, as clouds in the rainy season cover a mountain."}},{"n":21,"text":"स च्छाद्यमानो बहुधा पुत्रैस्तव विशां पते ।\nसृक्किणी विलिहन्वीरः शार्दूल इव दर्पितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Showered with arrows from many sides by your sons, lord of the people, that hero licked the corners of his mouth like a proud tiger."}},{"n":22,"text":"व्यूढोरस्कं ततो भीमः पातयामास पार्थिव ।\nक्षुरप्रेण सुतीक्ष्णेन सोऽभवद्गतजीवितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O king, Bhima felled with a sharp razor-headed arrow one broad-chested son of yours, who lost his life."}},{"n":23,"text":"अपरेण तु भल्लेन पीतेन निशितेन च ।\nअपातयत्कुण्डलिनं सिंहः क्षुद्रमृगं यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"With another keen, yellow-tinted broad-headed arrow he felled an earring-wearer, as a lion strikes a small deer."}},{"n":24,"text":"ततः सुनिशितान्पीतान्समादत्त शिलीमुखान् ।\nस सप्त त्वरया युक्तः पुत्रांस्ते प्राप्य मारिष ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, my lord, he took up seven sharp yellow arrows and swiftly aimed them at your sons."}},{"n":25,"text":"प्रेषिता भीमसेनेन शरास्ते दृढधन्वना ।\nअपातयन्त पुत्रांस्ते रथेभ्यः सुमहारथान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shot by the strong-bowed Bhimasena, those arrows threw your sons, great chariot-fighters, down from their chariots."}},{"n":26,"text":"अनाधृष्टिं कुण्डभेदं वैराटं दीर्घलोचनम् ।\nदीर्घबाहुं सुबाहुं च तथैव कनकध्वजम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Anadhrishti, Kundabhedin, Vairata, Dirghalochana, Dirghabahu, Subahu, and Kanakadhvaja too,"}},{"n":27,"text":"प्रपतन्त स्म ते वीरा विरेजुर्भरतर्षभ ।\nवसन्ते पुष्पशबलाश्चूताः प्रपतिता इव ॥","meaning":{"en":"those heroes fell and yet shone, bull of the Bharatas, like mango trees in spring, dotted with blossoms, that have fallen."}},{"n":28,"text":"ततः प्रदुद्रुवुः शेषाः पुत्रास्तव विशां पते ।\nतं कालमिव मन्यन्तो भीमसेनं महाबलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the rest of your sons fled, lord of the people, thinking mighty Bhimasena to be Death himself."}},{"n":29,"text":"द्रोणस्तु समरे वीरं निर्दहन्तं सुतांस्तव ।\nयथाद्रिं वारिधाराभिः समन्ताद्व्यकिरच्छरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Drona covered that hero, who was burning up your sons in battle, with arrows on every side, as streams of water pelt a mountain."}},{"n":30,"text":"तत्राद्भुतमपश्याम कुन्तीपुत्रस्य पौरुषम् ।\nद्रोणेन वार्यमाणोऽपि निजघ्ने यत्सुतांस्तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"There we saw a marvel of the son of Kunti's manliness: though Drona held him back, he still killed your sons."}},{"n":31,"text":"यथा हि गोवृषो वर्षं संधारयति खात्पतत् ।\nभीमस्तथा द्रोणमुक्तं शरवर्षमदीधरत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a bull bears the rain falling from the sky, so Bhima bore the shower of arrows loosed by Drona."}},{"n":32,"text":"अद्भुतं च महाराज तत्र चक्रे वृकोदरः ।\nयत्पुत्रांस्तेऽवधीत्संख्ये द्रोणं चैव न्ययोधयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"O great king, Vrikodara did a wonder there: he slew your sons in the fight and also fought Drona."}},{"n":33,"text":"पुत्रेषु तव वीरेषु चिक्रीडार्जुनपूर्वजः ।\nमृगेष्विव महाराज चरन्व्याघ्रो महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna's elder brother played among your heroic sons, like a mighty tiger roaming among deer."}},{"n":34,"text":"यथा वा पशुमध्यस्थो द्रावयेत पशून्वृकः ।\nवृकोदरस्तव सुतांस्तथा व्यद्रावयद्रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a wolf amid a herd scatters the cattle, so Vrikodara scattered your sons in the battle."}},{"n":35,"text":"गाङ्गेयो भगदत्तश्च गौतमश्च महारथः ।\nपाण्डवं रभसं युद्धे वारयामासुरर्जुनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The son of Ganga, Bhagadatta, and the great charioteer Kripa, son of Gautama, held back the furious Pandava Arjuna in the fight."}},{"n":36,"text":"अस्त्रैरस्त्राणि संवार्य तेषां सोऽतिरथो रणे ।\nप्रवीरांस्तव सैन्येषु प्रेषयामास मृत्यवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"That supreme chariot-warrior countered their weapons with his own and sent the finest heroes of your army to their deaths."}},{"n":37,"text":"अभिमन्युश्च राजानमम्बष्ठं लोकविश्रुतम् ।\nविरथं रथिनां श्रेष्ठं कारयामास सायकैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And Abhimanyu with his arrows made the world-famed king Ambashtha, best of charioteers, lose his chariot."}},{"n":38,"text":"विरथो वध्यमानः स सौभद्रेण यशस्विना ।\nअवप्लुत्य रथात्तूर्णं सव्रीडो मनुजाधिपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Deprived of his chariot and pressed by glorious Saubhadra, that king leapt quickly down from it, ashamed."}},{"n":39,"text":"असिं चिक्षेप समरे सौभद्रस्य महात्मनः ।\nआरुरोह रथं चैव हार्दिक्यस्य महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He hurled his sword at the great-souled son of Subhadra, and then mounted the chariot of the great-souled Hardikya."}},{"n":40,"text":"आपतन्तं तु निस्त्रिंशं युद्धमार्गविशारदः ।\nलाघवाद्व्यंसयामास सौभद्रः परवीरहा ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Saubhadra, slayer of enemy heroes, skilled in the ways of fighting, deftly turned aside the sword as it flew at him."}},{"n":41,"text":"व्यंसितं वीक्ष्य निस्त्रिंशं सौभद्रेण रणे तदा ।\nसाधु साध्विति सैन्यानां प्रणादोऽभूद्विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the sword thus turned aside by Saubhadra in the battle, a shout of \"Well done! Well done!\" rose from the armies, O lord of the people."}},{"n":42,"text":"धृष्टद्युम्नमुखास्त्वन्ये तव सैन्यमयोधयन् ।\nतथैव तावकाः सर्वे पाण्डुसैन्यमयोधयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Other warriors led by Dhrishtadyumna fought your army, and likewise all your men fought the Pandava army."}},{"n":43,"text":"तत्राक्रन्दो महानासीत्तव तेषां च भारत ।\nनिघ्नतां भृशमन्योन्यं कुर्वतां कर्म दुष्करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A great outcry arose there, Bharata, from your men and theirs, as they struck one another hard and did deeds hard to perform."}},{"n":44,"text":"अन्योन्यं हि रणे शूराः केशेष्वाक्षिप्य मारिष ।\nनखैर्दन्तैरयुध्यन्त मुष्टिभिर्जानुभिस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Heroes in that battle seized one another by the hair, my lord, and fought with nails, teeth, fists, and knees."}},{"n":45,"text":"बाहुभिश्च तलैश्चैव निस्त्रिंशैश्च सुसंशितैः ।\nविवरं प्राप्य चान्योन्यमनयन्यमसादनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With arms, with palms, and with well-sharpened swords, finding an opening, they sent one another to the abode of Yama."}},{"n":46,"text":"न्यहनच्च पिता पुत्रं पुत्रश्च पितरं रणे ।\nव्याकुलीकृतसंकल्पा युयुधुस्तत्र मानवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Father struck son and son struck father in the battle; the men fought with their judgment confused."}},{"n":47,"text":"रणे चारूणि चापानि हेमपृष्ठानि भारत ।\nहतानामपविद्धानि कलापाश्च महाधनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"On the field lay fine bows with golden backs thrown down by the slain, Bharata, and costly quivers."}},{"n":48,"text":"जातरूपमयैः पुङ्खै राजतैश्च शिताः शराः ।\nतैलधौता व्यराजन्त निर्मुक्तभुजगोपमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sharp arrows with feathers of gold and silver, washed in oil, shone like snakes that had shed their skins."}},{"n":49,"text":"हस्तिदन्तत्सरून्खड्गाञ्जातरूपपरिष्कृतान् ।\nचर्माणि चापविद्धानि रुक्मपृष्ठानि धन्विनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There lay swords with ivory hilts adorned with gold, and shields with golden backs, cast aside by the archers."}},{"n":50,"text":"सुवर्णविकृतप्रासान्पट्टिशान्हेमभूषितान् ।\nजातरूपमयाश्चर्ष्टीः शक्त्यश्च कनकोज्ज्वलाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There were javelins wrought with gold, clubs set with gold, golden battle-axes, and spears gleaming with gold."}},{"n":51,"text":"अपकृत्ताश्च पतिता मुसलानि गुरूणि च ।\nपरिघान्पट्टिशांश्चैव भिण्डिपालांश्च मारिष ॥","meaning":{"en":"Heavy maces lay fallen, my lord, together with severed iron clubs, battle-axes, and bhindipalas."}},{"n":52,"text":"पतितांस्तोमरांश्चापि चित्रा हेमपरिष्कृताः ।\nकुथाश्च बहुधाकाराश्चामरव्यजनानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fallen too were tomaras and varied gold-trimmed saddle-cloths of many kinds, with chowries and fans."}},{"n":53,"text":"नानाविधानि शस्त्राणि विसृज्य पतिता नराः ।\nजीवन्त इव दृश्यन्ते गतसत्त्वा महारथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Men who had dropped their many kinds of weapons lay fallen; those dead great chariot-fighters looked as if still alive."}},{"n":54,"text":"गदाविमथितैर्गात्रैर्मुसलैर्भिन्नमस्तकाः ।\nगजवाजिरथक्षुण्णाः शेरते स्म नराः क्षितौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Men lay on the ground with limbs crushed by maces, heads split by clubs, and bodies trampled by elephants, horses, and chariots."}},{"n":55,"text":"तथैवाश्वनृनागानां शरीरैराबभौ तदा ।\nसंछन्ना वसुधा राजन्पर्वतैरिव सर्वतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O king, the earth was covered everywhere with the bodies of horses, men, and elephants, as if with mountains."}},{"n":56,"text":"समरे पतितैश्चैव शक्त्यृष्टिशरतोमरैः ।\nनिस्त्रिंशैः पट्टिशैः प्रासैरयस्कुन्तैः परश्वधैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The ground was strewn with the fallen in the battle and with spears, darts, arrows, tomaras, swords, battle-axes, lances, iron-tipped pikes, and axes,"}},{"n":57,"text":"परिघैर्भिण्डिपालैश्च शतघ्नीभिस्तथैव च ।\nशरीरैः शस्त्रभिन्नैश्च समास्तीर्यत मेदिनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"with clubs, bhindipalas, and shataghnis, and with bodies cut by weapons."}},{"n":58,"text":"निःशब्दैरल्पशब्दैश्च शोणितौघपरिप्लुतैः ।\nगतासुभिरमित्रघ्न विबभौ संवृता मही ॥","meaning":{"en":"Slayer of foes, the earth shone, covered with the dead, silent or whimpering, drenched in floods of blood."}},{"n":59,"text":"सतलत्रैः सकेयूरैर्बाहुभिश्चन्दनोक्षितैः ।\nहस्तिहस्तोपमैश्छिन्नैरूरुभिश्च तरस्विनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arms with gloves and armlets, smeared with sandal and like elephants' trunks, and the severed thighs of the mighty lay about,"}},{"n":60,"text":"बद्धचूडामणिधरैः शिरोभिश्च सकुण्डलैः ।\nपतितैर्वृषभाक्षाणां बभौ भारत मेदिनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"along with heads with earrings and bound crest-jewels, with eyes like a bull's; so the earth shone, Bharata."}},{"n":61,"text":"कवचैः शोणितादिग्धैर्विप्रकीर्णैश्च काञ्चनैः ।\nरराज सुभृशं भूमिः शान्तार्चिभिरिवानलैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Armour smeared with blood and scattered golden ornaments made the ground gleam like fires whose flames have died down."}},{"n":62,"text":"विप्रविद्धैः कलापैश्च पतितैश्च शरासनैः ।\nविप्रकीर्णैः शरैश्चापि रुक्मपुङ्खैः समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Everywhere lay scattered quivers, fallen bows, and arrows with golden feathers strewn around."}},{"n":63,"text":"रथैश्च बहुभिर्भग्नैः किङ्किणीजालमालिभिः ।\nवाजिभिश्च हतैः कीर्णैः स्रस्तजिह्वैः सशोणितैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There were many shattered chariots hung with strings of tinkling bells, and slain horses with lolling tongues, scattered about and bloody."}},{"n":64,"text":"अनुकर्षैः पताकाभिरुपासङ्गैर्ध्वजैरपि ।\nप्रवीराणां महाशङ्खैर्विप्रकीर्णैश्च पाण्डुरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There were axle-supports, banners, saddle-bags, and standards, and the big white conches of the heroes lay scattered."}},{"n":65,"text":"स्रस्तहस्तैश्च मातङ्गैः शयानैर्विबभौ मही ।\nनानारूपैरलंकारैः प्रमदेवाभ्यलंकृता ॥","meaning":{"en":"With elephants lying prone, their trunks limp, the earth shone like a woman adorned with ornaments of every shape."}},{"n":66,"text":"दन्तिभिश्चापरैस्तत्र सप्रासैर्गाढवेदनैः ।\nकरैः शब्दं विमुञ्चद्भिः शीकरं च मुहुर्मुहुः ।\nविबभौ तद्रणस्थानं धम्यमानैरिवाचलैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Other elephants, pierced by spears and in deep pain, cried out with their trunks and again and again sprayed mist; that battlefield looked like mountains being blown upon."}},{"n":67,"text":"नानारागैः कम्बलैश्च परिस्तोमैश्च दन्तिनाम् ।\nवैडूर्यमणिदण्डैश्च पतितैरङ्कुशैः शुभैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There lay colourful blankets and elephant-housings, and fine goads with shafts of cat's-eye gems, fallen."}},{"n":68,"text":"घण्टाभिश्च गजेन्द्राणां पतिताभिः समन्ततः ।\nविघाटितविचित्राभिः कुथाभी राङ्कवैस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bells of the best elephants had fallen all around, and torn, many-coloured cloths and deerskin coverings."}},{"n":69,"text":"ग्रैवेयैश्चित्ररूपैश्च रुक्मकक्ष्याभिरेव च ।\nयन्त्रैश्च बहुधा छिन्नैस्तोमरैश्च सकम्पनैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There were collars of varied designs, golden girths, shattered machines, and quivering tomaras."}},{"n":70,"text":"अश्वानां रेणुकपिलै रुक्मच्छन्नैरुरश्छदैः ।\nसादिनां च भुजैश्छिन्नैः पतितैः साङ्गदैस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"There were golden breast-plates of horses, grey with dust, and the severed arms of horsemen, with their armlets, lay fallen."}},{"n":71,"text":"प्रासैश्च विमलैस्तीक्ष्णैर्विमलाभिस्तथर्ष्टिभिः ।\nउष्णीषैश्च तथा छिन्नैः प्रविद्धैश्च ततस्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There were bright, sharp spears and gleaming lances, and turbans cut off and flung here and there."}},{"n":72,"text":"विचित्रैरर्धचन्द्रैश्च जातरूपपरिष्कृतैः ।\nअश्वास्तरपरिस्तोमै राङ्कवैर्मृदितैस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"There were wonderful half-moon arrows set with gold, horse-blankets and coverings of deerskin trampled down."}},{"n":73,"text":"नरेन्द्रचूडामणिभिर्विचित्रैश्च महाधनैः ।\nछत्रैस्तथापविद्धैश्च चामरव्यजनैरपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"There were splendid, costly crest-jewels of kings, parasols thrown away, and chowries and fans."}},{"n":74,"text":"पद्मेन्दुद्युतिभिश्चैव वदनैश्चारुकुण्डलैः ।\nकॢप्तश्मश्रुभिरत्यर्थं वीराणां समलंकृतैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There were faces of heroes, bright as lotus or moon, with lovely earrings and carefully trimmed beards, ornamented."}},{"n":75,"text":"अपविद्धैर्महाराज सुवर्णोज्ज्वलकुण्डलैः ।\nग्रहनक्षत्रशबला द्यौरिवासीद्वसुंधरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Strewn with the gold-bright earrings flung off, great king, the earth looked like the sky mottled with planets and stars."}},{"n":76,"text":"एवमेते महासेने मृदिते तत्र भारत ।\nपरस्परं समासाद्य तव तेषां च संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus your two great armies, Bharata, ground each other down there in the fight when they met."}},{"n":77,"text":"तेषु श्रान्तेषु भग्नेषु मृदितेषु च भारत ।\nरात्रिः समभवद्घोरा नापश्याम ततो रणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When they were weary, broken, and crushed, Bharata, dreadful night fell and we could no longer see the battle."}},{"n":78,"text":"ततोऽवहारं सैन्यानां प्रचक्रुः कुरुपाण्डवाः ।\nघोरे निशामुखे रौद्रे वर्तमाने सुदारुणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the Kurus and Pandavas called off their armies, as the grim, terrible, fearsome nightfall came on."}},{"n":79,"text":"अवहारं ततः कृत्वा सहिताः कुरुपाण्डवाः ।\nन्यविशन्त यथाकालं गत्वा स्वशिबिरं तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having called back their troops, the Kurus and Pandavas together went at the proper time to their own camps and settled in."}}]}]}